<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <!--
      Android TV flavor overlay.

      leanback is REQUIRED here. That is deliberate and it is what the dedicated
      Android TV track demands:

        "APKs or Android App Bundles in this track must require the following
         features: android.software.leanback."

      Do not "fix" this back to false. The two Play errors are mirror images of
      each other and the correct value depends entirely on the track:

        Standard / mobile track -> leanback must NOT be required
          "APKs and bundles must not require following features:
           android.software.leanback. Some features can only be required in
           dedicated tracks."

        Dedicated Android TV track -> leanback MUST be required (this file)

      That is why the value lives in the flavor overlay and not in the main
      manifest: src/main stays required="false" so the mobile flavor remains
      valid on the standard track, and only this flavor flips it. android:required
      merges with a logical OR, so "true" here wins over the "false" in the main
      manifest without needing tools:replace.

      Requiring leanback is also what finally makes the two builds distinguishable
      to Play. Mobile and TV share applicationId cc.voltix.streaming and therefore
      one listing; with identical feature sets Play could not tell them apart and
      served whichever had the highest versionCode to every device. This build is
      now TV-only in Play's eyes.

      CONSEQUENCE: this flavor can ONLY be uploaded to the Android TV track. It
      will be rejected on the standard track.
    -->
    <uses-feature
        android:name="android.software.leanback"
        android:required="true" />

    <!-- Restated for clarity; TVs have no touchscreen. -->
    <uses-feature
        android:name="android.hardware.touchscreen"
        android:required="false" />

    <!--
      Restated from the main manifest. ACCESS_WIFI_STATE and
      CHANGE_WIFI_MULTICAST_STATE imply android.hardware.wifi, and an implied
      feature counts as REQUIRED unless declared otherwise - which filtered the
      app off Ethernet-only TV boxes. Kept here as well so the TV artifact is
      correct on its own terms.
    -->
    <uses-feature
        android:name="android.hardware.wifi"
        android:required="false" />

</manifest>
